{title: Come Let Us Join Our Friends Above}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Come, [C]let us join our [F]friends above, who [Dm]have obtained the [C]prize
And [C]on the eagle [F]wings of love to [Dm]joys celestial [C]rise
Let [G]saints, on earth u[F]nite to sing with [Am]those to glory [G]gone
For [C]all the servants [F]of our King in [Dm]earth and heaven are [C]one.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
One [C]family we [F]dwell in Him, one [Dm]church above, be[C]neath
Though [C]now divided [F]by the stream, the [Dm]narrow stream of [C]death
One [G]army of the [F]living God, to [Am]His command we [G]bow
Part [C]of His host have [F]crossed the flood, and [Dm]part are crossing [C]now.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Ten [C]thousand to their [F]endless home this [Dm]solemn moment [C]fly
And [C]we are to the [F]margin come, and [Dm]we expect to [C]die
E'en [G]now by faith we [F]join our hands, with [Am]those that went be[G]fore
And [C]greet the blood be [F]sprinkled bands, on [Dm]the eternal [C]shore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Our [C]spirits too shall [F]quickly join like [Dm]theirs with glory [C]crowned
And [C]shout to see our [F]Captain's sign, to [Dm]hear his trumpet [C]sound
O [G]that we now might [F]grasp our Guide! O [Am]that the word were [G]given
Come [C]Lord of Hosts the [F]waves divide and [Dm]land us all in [C]heaven
{end_of_verse}
